<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SOCCER-AFRICAN CLUB COMPETITION RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-AFRICAN CLUB COMPETITION RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of first round,</p>
<p>first leg matches in African club soccer competitions on</p>
<p>Saturday:</p>
<p>African Cup Winners' Cup</p>
<p>In Mumias, Kenya: Mumias Sugar (Kenya) 0 Arab Contractors</p>
<p>(Egypt, holders) 0</p>
<p>Attendance: 10,000</p>
<p>Champions' Cup</p>
<p>In Johannesburg:  Orlando Pirates (South Africa) 1 Roma Rovers (Lesotho) 0 (halftime 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Brandon Silent 32</p>
<p>Attendance: 20,000  </p>
<p>Confederation of African Football (CAF) Cup</p>
<p>In Marakesh: Kawkab Marakesh (Morocco) 1 ASC La Linguere (Senegal) 0 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Youssef el Amrani 66 penalty</p>
<p>Attendance: 4,000</p>
<p>In Bouake, Ivory Coast:  Stade Abidjan (Ivory Coast) 2 USFA (Burkina Faso) 3   (0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Stade Abidjan -- Yoruba Didie 70, 81</p>
<p>USFA -- Sanou Lazare 39, Salifou Traore 52, Romeo Kambou 89</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,000.  </p>
<p>African Cup Winners Cup</p>
<p>In Dakar: US Goreenne (Senegal) 1 Mouloudia Oran (Algeria) 0 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Gisele Sinou 89</p>
<p>Attendance: 8,000</p>
<p>In Libreville: FC 105 Libreville (Gabon) 2 Progresso (Angola) 0</p>
</text>
